PERSONNEL -- SAND HEADBAND (HITAI-ATE) ISSUANCE RECORD
Kazekage Office, Identity Division

The forehead protector bearing the hourglass mark of Sunagakure is issued upon a
recruit's graduation from the Academy and confirmation as a genin of the Sand.
It is both proof of allegiance and, in the field, a light protective plate.

Issuance rules:
- One protector per confirmed shinobi, engraved with the Sand symbol. Cloth
  color and wear-style are at the bearer's discretion within regulation.
- The protector is village property entrusted to the bearer. Its loss must be
  reported; its surrender or defacement is an act of desertion.
- A shinobi who abandons the village and scores the symbol is marked a
  missing-nin. The traitor Sasori's scored Sand plate stands as the byword.

Recovered protectors from the fallen are returned to this office for the
memorial register. New issuance is logged against the shinobi registration file.
Maintained under Identity Division seal.
